window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b308-43bb4beedab4af11.json"]={sha256:"43bb4beedab4af11645c0cf2541d8384f67819d95ccfc7628406c2d04eeaae42",value:{"id":"b308","title":"東北新幹線","titleEn":"Tohoku Shinkansen","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以東北新幹線向日本北部延伸的歷史為背景，設計積雪、低溫與側風並存的教學工況。分析防雪、黏著、道床熱量與輪軌監測之間的取捨，要求每項氣候假設均對應可量測的環境量。","summaryEn":"Use the northward development of the Tohoku Shinkansen to frame a teaching scenario combining snow, low temperature and crosswind. Examine tradeoffs among snow management, adhesion, thermal demand and wheel-rail monitoring. Every weather assumption must correspond to a measurable environmental quantity, and a successful single-condition test must be distinguished from validation across a winter operating envelope.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-highspeed","subcategoryTitle":"高速鐵路系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"High-speed rail systems","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-highspeed","learningTags":["rail","rail-highspeed","rail"],"architectureFamily":"rail-system","architectureNodes":[["路線與土建","Alignment and civil works"],["車輛與接觸","Vehicle and contact"],["牽引供電","Traction supply"],["行車控制","Movement control"],["車站與旅客","Stations and passengers"],["監測與維護","Monitoring and maintenance"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,1],[3,4],[4,5],[5,0],[5,3]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-system","labels":["路線與土建","車輛與接觸","牽引供電","行車控制","車站與旅客"],"labelsEn":["Alignment and civil works","Vehicle and contact","Traction supply","Movement control","Stations and passengers"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合原創算例：單元 1 得 melt_power=13.36 kW；單元 2 得 traction=162 kN；單元 3 得 moment=67.5 kN*m。上述三個結果使用各單元明示的不同邊界，不能任意相加或視為實際工程實測值。以第一單元 snow 的擾動測試，結果改為 14.696 kW；學徒需先比較單位、敏感度和假設，再決定是否要細化模型。以東北新幹線向日本北部延伸的歷史為背景，設計積雪、低溫與側風並存的教學工況。分析防雪、黏著、道床熱量與輪軌監測之間的取捨，要求每項氣候假設均對應可量測的環境量。 最終交付應保留原始輸入、測點時間戳、誤差範圍與無法由簡化式證明的結論。","textEn":"Integrated original exercise: unit 1 gives melt_power=13.36 kW; unit 2 gives traction=162 kN; unit 3 gives moment=67.5 kN*m. These three results use different explicit boundaries and must not be added or presented as measurements of the real railway. Perturbing snow in the first unit changes its result to 14.696 kW. Compare units, sensitivity and assumptions before deciding which model needs refinement. Use the northward development of the Tohoku Shinkansen to frame a teaching scenario combining snow, low temperature and crosswind. Examine tradeoffs among snow management, adhesion, thermal demand and wheel-rail monitoring. Every weather assumption must correspond to a measurable environmental quantity, and a successful single-condition test must be distinguished from validation across a winter operating envelope. The final submission should retain original inputs, measurement timestamps, uncertainty ranges and conclusions that the simplified expressions cannot establish.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b308-v16-s1","title":"融雪熱量與補給率與黏著限制與可用牽引力","titleEn":"Snow-melting heat and supply rate & Adhesion limit and usable traction","description":"本階段聚焦「融雪熱量與補給率」與「黏著限制與可用牽引力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Snow-melting heat and supply rate\" and \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b308-v16-01","title":"融雪熱量與補給率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Snow-melting heat and supply rate: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「融雪熱量與補給率」如何影響東北新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Snow-melting heat and supply rate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tohoku Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"把積雪融化需要先加熱到熔點再供應潛熱，若雪已在熔點則主要負荷是融化潛熱。積雪落在轉轍器附近會妨礙動作，融化後排水若再凍結也可能重新形成阻塞。 融雪至少要提供冰融化所需潛熱；若初溫低於冰點，還須先加熱到融點。此式僅算宣告的能量項，不能把理想加熱功率直接當成現場融雪產能。 把待融積雪質量與融雪能源分開量測，保留新雪補入量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「融雪熱量與補給率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Melting snow requires heating it to the melting point and supplying latent heat; snow already at that temperature mainly requires latent heat. Snow near point mechanisms can obstruct movement, while meltwater that refreezes may create another obstruction even after initial melting succeeds. Melting requires latent heat; snow initially below freezing must first be heated to the melting point. This expression includes only declared energy terms, so ideal heater power cannot be equated directly with field snow-removal capacity. Measure snow mass and melting energy separately while recording newly deposited snow. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Snow-melting heat and supply rate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：snow=0.04 kg/s; latent=334000 J/kg；計算：melt_power=snow*latent/1000=13.36 kW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: snow=0.04 kg/s; latent=334000 J/kg; calculation: melt_power=snow*latent/1000=13.36 kW.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要加熱器表面很熱就表示道岔冰雪問題已解決」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A hot heater surface proves that snow and ice obstruction at the points is resolved.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「融雪熱量與補給率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Snow-melting heat and supply rate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-01-k1","title":"融雪熱量與補給率","titleEn":"Snow-melting heat and supply rate","text":"把積雪融化需要先加熱到熔點再供應潛熱，若雪已在熔點則主要負荷是融化潛熱。積雪落在轉轍器附近會妨礙動作，融化後排水若再凍結也可能重新形成阻塞。","textEn":"Melting snow requires heating it to the melting point and supplying latent heat; snow already at that temperature mainly requires latent heat. Snow near point mechanisms can obstruct movement, while meltwater that refreezes may create another obstruction even after initial melting succeeds.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要加熱器表面很熱就表示道岔冰雪問題已解決 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A hot heater surface proves that snow and ice obstruction at the points is resolved. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「融雪熱量與補給率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Snow-melting heat and supply rate\" is correct?","options":["只要加熱器表面很熱就表示道岔冰雪問題已解決","把積雪融化需要先加熱到熔點再供應潛熱，若雪已在熔點則主要負荷是融化潛熱。","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著"],"optionsEn":["A hot heater surface proves that snow and ice obstruction at the points is resolved.","Melting snow requires heating it to the melting point and supplying latent heat; snow already at that temperature mainly requires latent heat.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把積雪融化需要先加熱到熔點再供應潛熱，若雪已在熔點則主要負荷是融化潛熱。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Melting snow requires heating it to the melting point and supplying latent heat; snow already at that temperature mainly requires latent heat. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b308-v16-02","title":"融雪熱量與補給率：定量估算","titleEn":"Snow-melting heat and supply rate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「融雪熱量與補給率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Snow-melting heat and supply rate” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：snow=0.04 kg/s; latent=334000 J/kg；計算：melt_power=snow*latent/1000=13.36 kW。敏感度：snow 單獨增加百分之十至 0.044 kg/s，其餘固定，結果為 14.696 kW。模型邊界：雪初溫為熔點且無環境散熱；僅理論潛熱功率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: snow=0.04 kg/s; latent=334000 J/kg; calculation: melt_power=snow*latent/1000=13.36 kW. Sensitivity: snow, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.044 kg/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 14.696 kW. Model boundary: Snow initially at melting point with no environmental losses; latent-heat power only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測進雪質量、融水流率及加熱電功率，記錄周圍溫度與風速，檢查能量帳和排水是否一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure snow mass input, meltwater flow and electrical heating power, log ambient temperature and wind, and check consistency of both the energy balance and drainage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：snow=0.04 kg/s; latent=334000 J/kg；計算：melt_power=snow*latent/1000=13.36 kW。敏感度：snow 單獨增加百分之十至 0.044 kg/s，其餘固定，結果為 14.696 kW。模型邊界：雪初溫為熔點且無環境散熱；僅理論潛熱功率。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: snow=0.04 kg/s; latent=334000 J/kg; calculation: melt_power=snow*latent/1000=13.36 kW. Sensitivity: snow, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.044 kg/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 14.696 kW. Model boundary: Snow initially at melting point with no environmental losses; latent-heat power only.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「融雪熱量與補給率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Snow-melting heat and supply rate\", which statement holds?","options":["隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口","完全拘束的鋼軌升溫仍會無應力地自由伸長","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：snow=0.04 kg/s; latent=334000 J/kg。"],"optionsEn":["A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.","A fully restrained rail still expands freely without stress when heated.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：snow=0.04 kg/s; latent=334000 J/kg；計算：melt_power=snow*latent/1000=13.36 kW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: snow=0.04 kg/s; latent=334000 J/kg; calculation: melt_power=snow*latent/1000=13.36 kW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b308-v16-03","title":"融雪熱量與補給率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Snow-melting heat and supply rate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「融雪熱量與補給率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Snow-melting heat and supply rate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測進雪質量、融水流率及加熱電功率，記錄周圍溫度與風速，檢查能量帳和排水是否一致。 先稱量積雪並量測初溫，核對加熱時間與電量，另記融水、散熱及持續降雪。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure snow mass input, meltwater flow and electrical heating power, log ambient temperature and wind, and check consistency of both the energy balance and drainage. Weigh the snow and measure its initial temperature, verify heating time and electricity, and separately record meltwater, heat loss and continuing snowfall. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：加入初始低於冰點的顯熱與散熱兩項需求，重新列出能量收支，並為排水再凍結設計獨立的觀察點。 再以本單元 snow 的對照值重算 melt_power，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Add sensible heating below freezing and environmental losses to the balance, then design an independent observation point for drainage refreezing. Also recalculate melt_power for the alternative snow value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：加熱器正常卻排水結冰時仍可能阻塞道岔；只量加熱器溫度不能確認冰雪已從關鍵間隙移除。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A working heater can coexist with frozen drainage and obstructed points; heater temperature alone does not prove snow has cleared the critical gap. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測進雪質量、融水流率及加熱電功率，記錄周圍溫度與風速，檢查能量帳和排水是否一致。 先稱量積雪並量測初溫，核對加熱時間與電量，另記融水、散熱及持續降雪。","textEn":"Measure snow mass input, meltwater flow and electrical heating power, log ambient temperature and wind, and check consistency of both the energy balance and drainage. Weigh the snow and measure its initial temperature, verify heating time and electricity, and separately record meltwater, heat loss and continuing snowfall.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"加入初始低於冰點的顯熱與散熱兩項需求，重新列出能量收支，並為排水再凍結設計獨立的觀察點。 再以本單元 snow 的對照值重算 melt_power，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Add sensible heating below freezing and environmental losses to the balance, then design an independent observation point for drainage refreezing. Also recalculate melt_power for the alternative snow value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「融雪熱量與補給率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Snow-melting heat and supply rate\"?","options":["量測進雪質量、融水流率及加熱電功率，記錄周圍溫度與風速，檢查能量帳和排水是否一致。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","頻譜中出現一個週期峰就一定證明軸承已損壞"],"optionsEn":["Measure snow mass input, meltwater flow and electrical heating power, log ambient temperature and wind, and check consistency of both the energy balance and drainage.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","One periodic spectral peak necessarily proves that a bearing is damaged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測進雪質量、融水流率及加熱電功率，記錄周圍溫度與風速，檢查能量帳和排水是否一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure snow mass input, meltwater flow and electrical heating power, log ambient temperature and wind, and check consistency of both the energy balance and drainage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b308-v16-04","title":"融雪熱量與補給率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Snow-melting heat and supply rate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「融雪熱量與補給率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Snow-melting heat and supply rate” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"加熱器正常卻排水結冰時仍可能阻塞道岔；只量加熱器溫度不能確認冰雪已從關鍵間隙移除。 新增降雪和散熱未計入時，融雪速度必然偏向理想值。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A working heater can coexist with frozen drainage and obstructed points; heater temperature alone does not prove snow has cleared the critical gap. Omitting new snowfall and heat loss biases the melting-rate estimate toward ideal conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把待融積雪質量與融雪能源分開量測，保留新雪補入量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Measure snow mass and melting energy separately while recording newly deposited snow.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要加熱器表面很熱就表示道岔冰雪問題已解決」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A hot heater surface proves that snow and ice obstruction at the points is resolved.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"加熱器正常卻排水結冰時仍可能阻塞道岔；只量加熱器溫度不能確認冰雪已從關鍵間隙移除。 新增降雪和散熱未計入時，融雪速度必然偏向理想值。","textEn":"A working heater can coexist with frozen drainage and obstructed points; heater temperature alone does not prove snow has cleared the critical gap. Omitting new snowfall and heat loss biases the melting-rate estimate toward ideal conditions.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「融雪熱量與補給率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Snow-melting heat and supply rate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","加熱器正常卻排水結冰時仍可能阻塞道岔；只量加熱器溫度不能確認冰雪已從關鍵間隙移除。","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A working heater can coexist with frozen drainage and obstructed points; heater temperature alone does not prove snow has cleared the critical gap.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"加熱器正常卻排水結冰時仍可能阻塞道岔；只量加熱器溫度不能確認冰雪已從關鍵間隙移除。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A working heater can coexist with frozen drainage and obstructed points; heater temperature alone does not prove snow has cleared the critical gap. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b308-v16-05","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「黏著限制與可用牽引力」如何影響東北新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Adhesion limit and usable traction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tohoku Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。電機能提供更大扭矩不代表輪軌能傳遞；雨水、落葉與速度都會改變接觸狀態，使固定係數模型失去精度。 法向荷重應只取實際驅動接觸點的總量，不能自動使用整列重量。此上限也不描述黏著峰後的滑移控制；若輪重轉移，就要以每個接觸點重新分配。 用濕軌與雪後工況比較可用牽引力，保留輪重分布。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「黏著限制與可用牽引力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Traction reaches the track through contact patches. A simple upper bound multiplies adhesion coefficient by normal force on driven wheels. More motor torque does not guarantee more transmitted force; rain, leaves and speed alter contact conditions and limit the accuracy of a fixed coefficient. Normal load must include only the driven contacts, not automatically the weight of the whole train. This bound does not describe slip control beyond the adhesion peak. Wheel-load transfer requires a new allocation across individual contact points. Compare traction bounds on wet and post-snow track while retaining wheel-load distribution. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Adhesion limit and usable traction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Adhesion limit and usable traction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-05-k1","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction","text":"牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。電機能提供更大扭矩不代表輪軌能傳遞；雨水、落葉與速度都會改變接觸狀態，使固定係數模型失去精度。","textEn":"Traction reaches the track through contact patches. A simple upper bound multiplies adhesion coefficient by normal force on driven wheels.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「黏著限制與可用牽引力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\" is correct?","options":["電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著","側風翻覆力矩只和風速成正比而不涉及車體高度","牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.","Crosswind overturning moment is linear in wind speed and independent of vehicle height.","Traction reaches the track through contact patches."],"answer":2,"explanation":"牽引力需要透過接觸斑傳到軌道，簡化上限與黏著係數及動輪法向力相乘。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Traction reaches the track through contact patches. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b308-v16-06","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：定量估算","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Adhesion limit and usable traction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN。敏感度：mu 單獨增加百分之十至 0.198 1，其餘固定，結果為 178.2 kN。模型邊界：準靜態庫倫上限與均勻輪重；未建模蠕滑曲線及動態減載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN. Sensitivity: mu, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.198 1, with all other inputs fixed, gives 178.2 kN. Model boundary: Quasi-static Coulomb bound with uniform wheel load; creep curves and dynamic unloading are not modelled. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN。敏感度：mu 單獨增加百分之十至 0.198 1，其餘固定，結果為 178.2 kN。模型邊界：準靜態庫倫上限與均勻輪重；未建模蠕滑曲線及動態減載。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN. Sensitivity: mu, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.198 1, with all other inputs fixed, gives 178.2 kN. Model boundary: Quasi-static Coulomb bound with uniform wheel load; creep curves and dynamic unloading are not modelled.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N。","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","量測車速度提高時仍可永遠沿用原本取樣率"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","The original sampling rate remains sufficient at every increased inspection speed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N；計算：traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: mu=0.18 1; weight=900000 N; calculation: traction=mu*weight/1000=162 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b308-v16-07","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「黏著限制與可用牽引力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Adhesion limit and usable traction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。 以獨立地速校對輪周速度，核實輪徑設定，再按乾濕條件與軸荷分類比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean. Calibrate wheel-periphery speed against independent ground speed, verify wheel-diameter settings, and compare results by wetness condition and axle load. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把黏著係數減半並比較動輪荷重調整，計算牽引上限，解釋為何撒砂或控制策略的效果需用試驗而不能只看馬達功率。 再以本單元 mu 的對照值重算 traction，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Halve adhesion and compare a change in driven-wheel load, calculate traction bounds, and explain why sanding or control performance requires tests rather than motor-power data alone. Also recalculate traction for the alternative mu value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。 以獨立地速校對輪周速度，核實輪徑設定，再按乾濕條件與軸荷分類比對。","textEn":"Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean. Calibrate wheel-periphery speed against independent ground speed, verify wheel-diameter settings, and compare results by wetness condition and axle load.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把黏著係數減半並比較動輪荷重調整，計算牽引上限，解釋為何撒砂或控制策略的效果需用試驗而不能只看馬達功率。 再以本單元 mu 的對照值重算 traction，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Halve adhesion and compare a change in driven-wheel load, calculate traction bounds, and explain why sanding or control performance requires tests rather than motor-power data alone. Also recalculate traction for the alternative mu value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「黏著限制與可用牽引力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較輪速、列車獨立速度與牽引電流，找出滑轉開始點；濕乾條件必須分組，不能用全日平均係數掩蓋低黏著尾端。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare wheel speed, independently measured train speed and traction current to locate slip onset, separating wet and dry conditions rather than hiding low-adhesion tails in a daily mean. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b308-v16-08","title":"黏著限制與可用牽引力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Adhesion limit and usable traction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「黏著限制與可用牽引力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Adhesion limit and usable traction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 先查輪徑與地速誤差，避免把量測偏差當成真滑轉。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. Check diameter and ground-speed errors before interpreting measurement bias as actual wheel slip. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：用濕軌與雪後工況比較可用牽引力，保留輪重分布。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare traction bounds on wet and post-snow track while retaining wheel-load distribution.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 先查輪徑與地速誤差，避免把量測偏差當成真滑轉。","textEn":"Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. Check diameter and ground-speed errors before interpreting measurement bias as actual wheel slip.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「黏著限制與可用牽引力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Adhesion limit and usable traction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","側風翻覆力矩只和風速成正比而不涉及車體高度","只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Crosswind overturning moment is linear in wind speed and independent of vehicle height.","Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只提高扭矩可能觸發滑轉並降低可控牽引；輪徑設定誤差也會製造假的滑差，需以獨立地速判別。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Increasing torque can trigger slip and reduce controllable traction; an incorrect wheel diameter also creates apparent slip, requiring independent ground-speed evidence. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b308-v16-s2","title":"側風力與翻覆力矩與隧道壓力波傳遞","titleEn":"Crosswind force and overturning moment & Tunnel pressure-wave travel","description":"本階段聚焦「側風力與翻覆力矩」與「隧道壓力波傳遞」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Crosswind force and overturning moment\" and \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b308-v16-09","title":"側風力與翻覆力矩：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Crosswind force and overturning moment: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「側風力與翻覆力矩」如何影響東北新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Crosswind force and overturning moment” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tohoku Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"側風作用可由動壓乘有效側向面積估算，再乘作用高度形成翻覆力矩。車輛質量、重心、風向及橋面遮蔽同時影響輪重分配，單一靜態力矩只能提供比較而非營運風速門檻。 橫向力依側風分量平方變化，列車姿態和地形會改變受風面積及係數。此力尺度不直接給出傾覆門檻；還需重心、輪重減載、懸吊和陣風時間歷程。 把側風平均值與陣風峰值分開，檢查兩種量測時間尺度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「側風力與翻覆力矩」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Crosswind force can be estimated from dynamic pressure and effective lateral area, then multiplied by application height for an overturning moment. Mass, centre of gravity, wind direction and shielding affect wheel loading together; one static moment only supports comparison, not an operational wind threshold. Lateral force varies with squared crosswind component, while vehicle attitude and terrain change exposed area and coefficients. The force scale does not directly yield an overturning threshold; centre of gravity, wheel unloading, suspension and gust history remain necessary. Separate mean crosswind and gust peaks and examine their different measurement timescales. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Crosswind force and overturning moment” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1.2 kg/m^3; wind=25 m/s; side_area=90 m^2; coefficient=1 1; height=2 m；計算：moment=0.5*rho*wind**2*side_area*coefficient*height/1000=67.5 kN*m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: rho=1.2 kg/m^3; wind=25 m/s; side_area=90 m^2; coefficient=1 1; height=2 m; calculation: moment=0.5*rho*wind**2*side_area*coefficient*height/1000=67.5 kN*m.","failure":"常見誤解：「側風翻覆力矩只和風速成正比而不涉及車體高度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Crosswind overturning moment is linear in wind speed and independent of vehicle height.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「側風力與翻覆力矩」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Crosswind force and overturning moment”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-09-k1","title":"側風力與翻覆力矩","titleEn":"Crosswind force and overturning moment","text":"側風作用可由動壓乘有效側向面積估算，再乘作用高度形成翻覆力矩。車輛質量、重心、風向及橋面遮蔽同時影響輪重分配，單一靜態力矩只能提供比較而非營運風速門檻。","textEn":"Crosswind force can be estimated from dynamic pressure and effective lateral area, then multiplied by application height for an overturning moment. Mass, centre of gravity, wind direction and shielding affect wheel loading together; one static moment only supports comparison, not an operational wind threshold.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：側風翻覆力矩只和風速成正比而不涉及車體高度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Crosswind overturning moment is linear in wind speed and independent of vehicle height. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「側風力與翻覆力矩」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Crosswind force and overturning moment\" is correct?","options":["側風作用可由動壓乘有效側向面積估算，再乘作用高度形成翻覆力矩。","側風翻覆力矩只和風速成正比而不涉及車體高度","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["Crosswind force can be estimated from dynamic pressure and effective lateral area, then multiplied by application height for an overturning moment.","Crosswind overturning moment is linear in wind speed and independent of vehicle height.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":0,"explanation":"側風作用可由動壓乘有效側向面積估算，再乘作用高度形成翻覆力矩。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Crosswind force can be estimated from dynamic pressure and effective lateral area, then multiplied by application height for an overturning moment. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b308-v16-10","title":"側風力與翻覆力矩：定量估算","titleEn":"Crosswind force and overturning moment: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「側風力與翻覆力矩」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Crosswind force and overturning moment” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1.2 kg/m^3; wind=25 m/s; side_area=90 m^2; coefficient=1 1; height=2 m；計算：moment=0.5*rho*wind**2*side_area*coefficient*height/1000=67.5 kN*m。敏感度：wind 單獨增加百分之十至 27.5 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 81.675 kN*m。模型邊界：定常橫風與已假設氣動係數；不含陣風、列車運動與動態輪重減載。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: rho=1.2 kg/m^3; wind=25 m/s; side_area=90 m^2; coefficient=1 1; height=2 m; calculation: moment=0.5*rho*wind**2*side_area*coefficient*height/1000=67.5 kN*m. Sensitivity: wind, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 27.5 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 81.675 kN*m. Model boundary: Steady crosswind and assumed aerodynamic coefficient; gusts, train motion and dynamic unloading are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記錄沿線風速、風向、列車速度及車體側滾，檢查風速站是否受地形遮蔽，再用多點資料評估代表性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise wind speed, direction, train speed and carbody roll, inspect terrain shielding at the anemometer, and assess representativeness with multiple locations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1.2 kg/m^3; wind=25 m/s; side_area=90 m^2; coefficient=1 1; height=2 m；計算：moment=0.5*rho*wind**2*side_area*coefficient*height/1000=67.5 kN*m。敏感度：wind 單獨增加百分之十至 27.5 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 81.675 kN*m。模型邊界：定常橫風與已假設氣動係數；不含陣風、列車運動與動態輪重減載。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: rho=1.2 kg/m^3; wind=25 m/s; side_area=90 m^2; coefficient=1 1; height=2 m; calculation: moment=0.5*rho*wind**2*side_area*coefficient*height/1000=67.5 kN*m. Sensitivity: wind, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 27.5 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 81.675 kN*m. Model boundary: Steady crosswind and assumed aerodynamic coefficient; gusts, train motion and dynamic unloading are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「側風力與翻覆力矩」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Crosswind force and overturning moment\", which statement holds?","options":["完全拘束的鋼軌升溫仍會無應力地自由伸長","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1.2 kg/m^3; wind=25 m/s; side_area=90 m^2; coefficient=1 1; height=2 m。","頻譜中出現一個週期峰就一定證明軸承已損壞"],"optionsEn":["A fully restrained rail still expands freely without stress when heated.","Original hypothetical exercise.","One periodic spectral peak necessarily proves that a bearing is damaged."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1.2 kg/m^3; wind=25 m/s; side_area=90 m^2; coefficient=1 1; height=2 m；計算：moment=0.5*rho*wind**2*side_area*coefficient*height/1000=67.5 kN*m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: rho=1.2 kg/m^3; wind=25 m/s; side_area=90 m^2; coefficient=1 1; height=2 m; calculation: moment=0.5*rho*wind**2*side_area*coefficient*height/1000=67.5 kN*m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b308-v16-11","title":"側風力與翻覆力矩：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Crosswind force and overturning moment: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「側風力與翻覆力矩」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Crosswind force and overturning moment” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記錄沿線風速、風向、列車速度及車體側滾，檢查風速站是否受地形遮蔽，再用多點資料評估代表性。 核對風速計高度與方向，保存陣風時序，將列車姿態與側向加速度放在同一時間軸。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise wind speed, direction, train speed and carbody roll, inspect terrain shielding at the anemometer, and assess representativeness with multiple locations. Verify anemometer height and orientation, retain gust histories, and align vehicle attitude with lateral acceleration on one timeline. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把風速與作用高度各增加一成，對比力矩敏感度，提出能區分地形加速與儀器誤差的多點量測配置。 再以本單元 wind 的對照值重算 moment，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase wind speed and load height separately by ten percent, compare moment sensitivity, and propose measurements distinguishing terrain acceleration from instrument error. Also recalculate moment for the alternative wind value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：受遮蔽的風速計可能低估橋上曝露，空載與滿載車又具有不同抗翻覆力矩；不能只用最近測站單一讀值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A sheltered anemometer can understate exposure on a viaduct, and empty versus loaded vehicles have different restoring moments; the nearest sensor alone is insufficient. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記錄沿線風速、風向、列車速度及車體側滾，檢查風速站是否受地形遮蔽，再用多點資料評估代表性。 核對風速計高度與方向，保存陣風時序，將列車姿態與側向加速度放在同一時間軸。","textEn":"Synchronise wind speed, direction, train speed and carbody roll, inspect terrain shielding at the anemometer, and assess representativeness with multiple locations. Verify anemometer height and orientation, retain gust histories, and align vehicle attitude with lateral acceleration on one timeline.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把風速與作用高度各增加一成，對比力矩敏感度，提出能區分地形加速與儀器誤差的多點量測配置。 再以本單元 wind 的對照值重算 moment，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase wind speed and load height separately by ten percent, compare moment sensitivity, and propose measurements distinguishing terrain acceleration from instrument error. Also recalculate moment for the alternative wind value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「側風力與翻覆力矩」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Crosswind force and overturning moment\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好","同步記錄沿線風速、風向、列車速度及車體側滾，檢查風速站是否受地形遮蔽，再用多點資料評估代表性。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition.","Synchronise wind speed, direction, train speed and carbody roll, inspect terrain shielding at the anemometer, and assess representativeness with multiple locations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步記錄沿線風速、風向、列車速度及車體側滾，檢查風速站是否受地形遮蔽，再用多點資料評估代表性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise wind speed, direction, train speed and carbody roll, inspect terrain shielding at the anemometer, and assess representativeness with multiple locations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b308-v16-12","title":"側風力與翻覆力矩：失效診斷","titleEn":"Crosswind force and overturning moment: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「側風力與翻覆力矩」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Crosswind force and overturning moment” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"受遮蔽的風速計可能低估橋上曝露，空載與滿載車又具有不同抗翻覆力矩；不能只用最近測站單一讀值。 日平均風速會掩蓋陣風，需檢查量測平均時間與峰值。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A sheltered anemometer can understate exposure on a viaduct, and empty versus loaded vehicles have different restoring moments; the nearest sensor alone is insufficient. Daily mean wind hides gusts; inspect averaging duration and the recorded peaks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把側風平均值與陣風峰值分開，檢查兩種量測時間尺度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Separate mean crosswind and gust peaks and examine their different measurement timescales.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「側風翻覆力矩只和風速成正比而不涉及車體高度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Crosswind overturning moment is linear in wind speed and independent of vehicle height.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"受遮蔽的風速計可能低估橋上曝露，空載與滿載車又具有不同抗翻覆力矩；不能只用最近測站單一讀值。 日平均風速會掩蓋陣風，需檢查量測平均時間與峰值。","textEn":"A sheltered anemometer can understate exposure on a viaduct, and empty versus loaded vehicles have different restoring moments; the nearest sensor alone is insufficient. Daily mean wind hides gusts; inspect averaging duration and the recorded peaks.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側風力與翻覆力矩」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Crosswind force and overturning moment\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["受遮蔽的風速計可能低估橋上曝露，空載與滿載車又具有不同抗翻覆力矩；不能只用最近測站單一讀值。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["A sheltered anemometer can understate exposure on a viaduct, and empty versus loaded vehicles have different restoring moments.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":0,"explanation":"受遮蔽的風速計可能低估橋上曝露，空載與滿載車又具有不同抗翻覆力矩；不能只用最近測站單一讀值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A sheltered anemometer can understate exposure on a viaduct, and empty versus loaded vehicles have different restoring moments; the nearest sensor alone is insufficient. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b308-v16-13","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「隧道壓力波傳遞」如何影響東北新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tohoku Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。入口緩衝設計影響波形上升率，波到達出口的時間與車身到達時間屬不同問題，須分開建立量測觸發。 波傳時間由傳播距離除以聲速決定，與列車走完整段的時間不同。此式只預測到達時序而不預測波幅；洞口形狀、列車頭型和反射決定的壓力變化須用其他流動模型。 在連續隧道與洞口測點之間比較聲波傳播時間和列車通過時間，另列波幅問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「隧道壓力波傳遞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. Entrance treatments affect the rise of the waveform. Wave arrival and train arrival are different events and require separate measurement triggers. Wave travel time is propagation distance divided by sound speed, not the time for the train to traverse the section. This expression predicts arrival timing, not amplitude. Portal geometry, train-nose shape and reflections require additional flow models to predict pressure changes. Compare acoustic travel time with train-passage time between tunnel and portal sensors, treating wave amplitude as a separate problem. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.352941 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.352941 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「隧道壓力波傳遞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tunnel pressure-wave travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-13-k1","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel","text":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。入口緩衝設計影響波形上升率，波到達出口的時間與車身到達時間屬不同問題，須分開建立量測觸發。","textEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. Entrance treatments affect the rise of the waveform.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隧道壓力波傳遞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\" is correct?","options":["隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口","列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下"],"optionsEn":["A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.","A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking."],"answer":1,"explanation":"列車鼻部入隧道產生壓縮擾動，壓力波以接近音速傳播而不是跟著列車速度前進。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A train nose entering a tunnel creates a compression disturbance whose propagation speed is close to acoustic speed rather than train speed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b308-v16-14","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：定量估算","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隧道壓力波傳遞」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.352941 s。敏感度：length 單獨增加百分之十至 2750 m，其餘固定，結果為 8.088235 s。模型邊界：一維線性聲學且音速均勻；不預測波幅、微壓波峰值或反射耗散。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.352941 s. Sensitivity: length, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2750 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.088235 s. Model boundary: One-dimensional linear acoustics with uniform sound speed; amplitude, micro-pressure-wave peaks and reflection losses are not predicted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.352941 s。敏感度：length 單獨增加百分之十至 2750 m，其餘固定，結果為 8.088235 s。模型邊界：一維線性聲學且音速均勻；不預測波幅、微壓波峰值或反射耗散。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.352941 s. Sensitivity: length, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 2750 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.088235 s. Model boundary: One-dimensional linear acoustics with uniform sound speed; amplitude, micro-pressure-wave peaks and reflection losses are not predicted.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「隧道壓力波傳遞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\", which statement holds?","options":["量測車速度提高時仍可永遠沿用原本取樣率","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["The original sampling rate remains sufficient at every increased inspection speed.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s；計算：travel=length/sound=7.352941 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=2500 m; sound=340 m/s; calculation: travel=length/sound=7.352941 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b308-v16-15","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隧道壓力波傳遞」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 在洞口與洞內配置同步壓力測點，對照列車頭部通過時刻，分辨首波與後續反射。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Synchronise pressure sensors at the portal and inside the tunnel with nose-passage time, distinguishing the first wave from later reflections. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較壓力波與列車兩種到達時間，加入一次端部反射畫出事件圖，說明單一延遲量無法判斷出口微壓波是否超標。 再以本單元 length 的對照值重算 travel，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare wave and train arrival times, add one end reflection to the event diagram, and explain why travel time alone cannot establish compliance of portal micro-pressure waves. Also recalculate travel for the alternative length value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 在洞口與洞內配置同步壓力測點，對照列車頭部通過時刻，分辨首波與後續反射。","textEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Synchronise pressure sensors at the portal and inside the tunnel with nose-passage time, distinguishing the first wave from later reflections.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較壓力波與列車兩種到達時間，加入一次端部反射畫出事件圖，說明單一延遲量無法判斷出口微壓波是否超標。 再以本單元 length 的對照值重算 travel，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare wave and train arrival times, add one end reflection to the event diagram, and explain why travel time alone cannot establish compliance of portal micro-pressure waves. Also recalculate travel for the alternative length value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「隧道壓力波傳遞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\"?","options":["在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要加熱器表面很熱就表示道岔冰雪問題已解決"],"optionsEn":["Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A hot heater surface proves that snow and ice obstruction at the points is resolved."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在入口與出口配置同步壓力計，用互相關估計傳遞時間，並用溫度估算音速；列車里程觸發另存一條通道。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use synchronised pressure sensors at both portals, estimate travel time by cross-correlation and sound speed from temperature, and retain train-position triggering separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b308-v16-16","title":"隧道壓力波傳遞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tunnel pressure-wave travel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隧道壓力波傳遞」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tunnel pressure-wave travel” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 單點峰值不足以判別首波，須檢查測點間傳遞時差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single peak cannot identify the first wave; inspect propagation delay between sensors. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在連續隧道與洞口測點之間比較聲波傳播時間和列車通過時間，另列波幅問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare acoustic travel time with train-passage time between tunnel and portal sensors, treating wave amplitude as a separate problem.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 單點峰值不足以判別首波，須檢查測點間傳遞時差。","textEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. A single peak cannot identify the first wave; inspect propagation delay between sensors.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「隧道壓力波傳遞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tunnel pressure-wave travel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking."],"answer":1,"explanation":"時間戳誤差會被誤認為波速變化；長隧道的反射波與多車事件也可能讓互相關找到錯誤的峰。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Timestamp error can imitate a wave-speed change, while reflected waves and multiple train events can make cross-correlation select the wrong peak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b308-v16-s3","title":"地震偵測提前量與長軌溫升與受限熱應力","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time & Long-rail temperature and restrained stress","description":"本階段聚焦「地震偵測提前量」與「長軌溫升與受限熱應力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Seismic detection lead time\" and \"Long-rail temperature and restrained stress\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b308-v16-17","title":"地震偵測提前量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「地震偵測提前量」如何影響東北新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Seismic detection lead time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tohoku Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。距離太近時提前量可能為負，警報並不能讓列車瞬間停止。 此處以相同距離比較兩種波速，屬簡化幾何模型。實際感測站可能不在線路與震源之間；可用時間還包括資料品質檢查及保護命令發送，不能只比較波速。 在警報訊號鏈加入低溫設備延遲，與波到達時間比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地震偵測提前量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay. A nearby source may leave negative lead time. An alarm therefore cannot make a moving train stop instantaneously, even when the detection itself works correctly. The exercise compares two wave speeds over the same distance and therefore uses simplified geometry. A real sensor may not lie between the source and railway. Available time also includes data-quality checks and protection-command delivery, not only wave propagation. Add cold-equipment delay to the alarm chain and compare it with wave-arrival time. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Seismic detection lead time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=100000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=9.904762 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=100000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=9.904762 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地震偵測提前量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Seismic detection lead time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-17-k1","title":"地震偵測提前量","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time","text":"地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。距離太近時提前量可能為負，警報並不能讓列車瞬間停止。","textEn":"Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay. A nearby source may leave negative lead time.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地震偵測提前量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Seismic detection lead time\" is correct?","options":["地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","完全拘束的鋼軌升溫仍會無應力地自由伸長","地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。"],"optionsEn":["A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","A fully restrained rail still expands freely without stress when heated.","Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay."],"answer":2,"explanation":"地震警報的可用提前量來自較快波到達感測點與較慢強震波到達設施之間的差，再扣掉傳輸和判定延遲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Usable seismic lead time is the difference between faster-wave detection and slower damaging-wave arrival, less communication and decision delay. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b308-v16-18","title":"地震偵測提前量：定量估算","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地震偵測提前量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Seismic detection lead time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=100000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=9.904762 s。敏感度：distance 單獨增加百分之十至 110000 m，其餘固定，結果為 11.09524 s。模型邊界：共線源站幾何與固定波速；不預測震度或實際地震動。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=100000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=9.904762 s. Sensitivity: distance, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 110000 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 11.09524 s. Model boundary: Collinear source-station geometry and constant wave speeds; neither intensity nor actual ground motion is predicted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=100000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=9.904762 s。敏感度：distance 單獨增加百分之十至 110000 m，其餘固定，結果為 11.09524 s。模型邊界：共線源站幾何與固定波速；不預測震度或實際地震動。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=100000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=9.904762 s. Sensitivity: distance, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 110000 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 11.09524 s. Model boundary: Collinear source-station geometry and constant wave speeds; neither intensity nor actual ground motion is predicted.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地震偵測提前量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Seismic detection lead time\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=100000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s。","頻譜中出現一個週期峰就一定證明軸承已損壞","濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","One periodic spectral peak necessarily proves that a bearing is damaged.","Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：distance=100000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s；計算：lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=9.904762 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: distance=100000 m; vp=6000 m/s; vs=3500 m/s; latency=2 s; calculation: lead=distance/vs-distance/vp-latency=9.904762 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b308-v16-19","title":"地震偵測提前量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地震偵測提前量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Seismic detection lead time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。 以完整訊號重播核對每個時間戳，將總延遲分解成判定、網路與列車端處理。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution. Use full-chain signal replay to verify every timestamp and separate total delay into decision, network and train-side processing components. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將震源距離縮短並把通訊延遲加倍，計算剩餘提前量；與制動時間比較，提出只在模型範圍內成立的結論。 再以本單元 distance 的對照值重算 lead，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Shorten source distance and double communication delay, calculate remaining lead time, and compare it with braking time without extending the conclusion beyond the model. Also recalculate lead for the alternative distance value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。 以完整訊號重播核對每個時間戳，將總延遲分解成判定、網路與列車端處理。","textEn":"Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution. Use full-chain signal replay to verify every timestamp and separate total delay into decision, network and train-side processing components.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將震源距離縮短並把通訊延遲加倍，計算剩餘提前量；與制動時間比較，提出只在模型範圍內成立的結論。 再以本單元 distance 的對照值重算 lead，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Shorten source distance and double communication delay, calculate remaining lead time, and compare it with braking time without extending the conclusion beyond the model. Also recalculate lead for the alternative distance value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地震偵測提前量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Seismic detection lead time\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用歷史或合成波形重播整條訊號鏈，記錄偵測、判定、通訊及列車接收時間，量出漏警、誤警和延遲分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Replay historical or synthetic waveforms through the complete chain, log detection, decision, communication and train receipt times, and measure missed alarms, false alarms and latency distribution. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b308-v16-20","title":"地震偵測提前量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Seismic detection lead time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地震偵測提前量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Seismic detection lead time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 感測成功不等於制動成功，須查列車收到命令後的動作。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. Successful detection is not successful braking; inspect the train response after command receipt. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在警報訊號鏈加入低溫設備延遲，與波到達時間比較。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Add cold-equipment delay to the alarm chain and compare it with wave-arrival time.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 感測成功不等於制動成功，須查列車收到命令後的動作。","textEn":"Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. Successful detection is not successful braking; inspect the train response after command receipt.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地震偵測提前量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Seismic detection lead time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","完全拘束的鋼軌升溫仍會無應力地自由伸長","只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A fully restrained rail still expands freely without stress when heated.","Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只驗證感測器觸發而不驗證下游通訊，可能高估提前量；設備共用電源也可能讓兩條名義獨立通道同時失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Testing the sensor without downstream communication overestimates lead time; a shared power supply can also defeat nominally independent channels simultaneously. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b308-v16-21","title":"長軌溫升與受限熱應力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Long-rail temperature and restrained stress: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「長軌溫升與受限熱應力」如何影響東北新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Long-rail temperature and restrained stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tohoku Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"自由鋼軌升溫會伸長，完全拘束的理想鋼軌則把熱應變轉成壓應力。鎖定軌溫決定應力零點而空氣溫度不等於鋼軌溫度；實際扣件滑移與軌道側向阻力還會改變穩定問題。 溫差應相對於鋼軌實際無應力狀態，而非任意室溫。完全拘束估算給出軸向應力尺度；當扣件滑移或軌道彎曲出現時，需要位移相容和側向穩定分析。 檢查寒冬鋼軌降溫時應力方向與夏季熱壓縮的差別。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「長軌溫升與受限熱應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A free rail expands on heating, while an ideally restrained rail converts thermal strain into compression. Stress-free rail temperature defines the reference and differs from air temperature. Fastener slip and lateral track resistance additionally govern stability, beyond the one-dimensional thermal-stress estimate. Temperature change must reference the rail’s actual stress-free state, not an arbitrary room temperature. Full restraint gives an axial stress scale. Fastener slip or track curvature requires displacement compatibility and lateral stability analysis beyond this expression. Examine the stress sign during winter cooling and contrast it with summer compression. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Long-rail temperature and restrained stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：E=210000 MPa; alpha=1.15e-05 1/K; deltaT=30 K；計算：compression=E*alpha*deltaT=72.45 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: E=210000 MPa; alpha=1.15e-05 1/K; deltaT=30 K; calculation: compression=E*alpha*deltaT=72.45 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「完全拘束的鋼軌升溫仍會無應力地自由伸長」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A fully restrained rail still expands freely without stress when heated.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「長軌溫升與受限熱應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Long-rail temperature and restrained stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-21-k1","title":"長軌溫升與受限熱應力","titleEn":"Long-rail temperature and restrained stress","text":"自由鋼軌升溫會伸長，完全拘束的理想鋼軌則把熱應變轉成壓應力。鎖定軌溫決定應力零點而空氣溫度不等於鋼軌溫度；實際扣件滑移與軌道側向阻力還會改變穩定問題。","textEn":"A free rail expands on heating, while an ideally restrained rail converts thermal strain into compression. Stress-free rail temperature defines the reference and differs from air temperature.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：完全拘束的鋼軌升溫仍會無應力地自由伸長 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A fully restrained rail still expands freely without stress when heated. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「長軌溫升與受限熱應力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long-rail temperature and restrained stress\" is correct?","options":["自由鋼軌升溫會伸長，完全拘束的理想鋼軌則把熱應變轉成壓應力。","完全拘束的鋼軌升溫仍會無應力地自由伸長","量測車速度提高時仍可永遠沿用原本取樣率"],"optionsEn":["A free rail expands on heating, while an ideally restrained rail converts thermal strain into compression.","A fully restrained rail still expands freely without stress when heated.","The original sampling rate remains sufficient at every increased inspection speed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"自由鋼軌升溫會伸長，完全拘束的理想鋼軌則把熱應變轉成壓應力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A free rail expands on heating, while an ideally restrained rail converts thermal strain into compression. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b308-v16-22","title":"長軌溫升與受限熱應力：定量估算","titleEn":"Long-rail temperature and restrained stress: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「長軌溫升與受限熱應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Long-rail temperature and restrained stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：E=210000 MPa; alpha=1.15e-05 1/K; deltaT=30 K；計算：compression=E*alpha*deltaT=72.45 MPa。敏感度：deltaT 單獨增加百分之十至 33 K，其餘固定，結果為 79.695 MPa。模型邊界：完全軸向拘束與線彈性；不計挫曲、初彎、殘留應力及塑性。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: E=210000 MPa; alpha=1.15e-05 1/K; deltaT=30 K; calculation: compression=E*alpha*deltaT=72.45 MPa. Sensitivity: deltaT, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 33 K, with all other inputs fixed, gives 79.695 MPa. Model boundary: Full axial restraint and linear elasticity; buckling, initial curvature, residual stress and plasticity are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量鋼軌本體溫度與縱向應變，記錄鎖定狀態和扣件維修歷程，用不同位置感測器區分局部溫差與整段受限變形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure rail temperature and longitudinal strain, record the fastening and maintenance history, and use spatially separated sensors to distinguish local heating from restrained segment behaviour.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：E=210000 MPa; alpha=1.15e-05 1/K; deltaT=30 K；計算：compression=E*alpha*deltaT=72.45 MPa。敏感度：deltaT 單獨增加百分之十至 33 K，其餘固定，結果為 79.695 MPa。模型邊界：完全軸向拘束與線彈性；不計挫曲、初彎、殘留應力及塑性。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: E=210000 MPa; alpha=1.15e-05 1/K; deltaT=30 K; calculation: compression=E*alpha*deltaT=72.45 MPa. Sensitivity: deltaT, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 33 K, with all other inputs fixed, gives 79.695 MPa. Model boundary: Full axial restraint and linear elasticity; buckling, initial curvature, residual stress and plasticity are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「長軌溫升與受限熱應力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long-rail temperature and restrained stress\", which statement holds?","options":["速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：E=210000 MPa; alpha=1.15e-05 1/K; deltaT=30 K。","只要加熱器表面很熱就表示道岔冰雪問題已解決"],"optionsEn":["A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A hot heater surface proves that snow and ice obstruction at the points is resolved."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：E=210000 MPa; alpha=1.15e-05 1/K; deltaT=30 K；計算：compression=E*alpha*deltaT=72.45 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: E=210000 MPa; alpha=1.15e-05 1/K; deltaT=30 K; calculation: compression=E*alpha*deltaT=72.45 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b308-v16-23","title":"長軌溫升與受限熱應力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long-rail temperature and restrained stress: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「長軌溫升與受限熱應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Long-rail temperature and restrained stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量鋼軌本體溫度與縱向應變，記錄鎖定狀態和扣件維修歷程，用不同位置感測器區分局部溫差與整段受限變形。 以鋼軌接觸式溫度計校驗遙測值，核對應變零點，並保留日夜循環的升降溫路徑。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure rail temperature and longitudinal strain, record the fastening and maintenance history, and use spatially separated sensors to distinguish local heating from restrained segment behaviour. Calibrate remote readings against a contact rail thermometer, verify strain zero, and retain heating and cooling paths across the daily cycle. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出自由、部分拘束與完全拘束三種邊界，重算熱變形或應力，標明哪些輸入必須由鋼軌溫度及扣件試驗取得。 再以本單元 deltaT 的對照值重算 compression，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw free, partial and full restraint boundaries, recalculate expansion or stress, and identify inputs requiring rail-temperature measurements and fastener tests. Also recalculate compression for the alternative deltaT value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：把氣溫直接當成鋼軌溫度會錯估熱荷載；扣件鬆動可能降低局部軸力卻增加位移，不能據此宣稱整體穩定性改善。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Substituting air temperature misstates thermal loading; loose fasteners may reduce local force while increasing displacement, which does not prove improved overall stability. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量鋼軌本體溫度與縱向應變，記錄鎖定狀態和扣件維修歷程，用不同位置感測器區分局部溫差與整段受限變形。 以鋼軌接觸式溫度計校驗遙測值，核對應變零點，並保留日夜循環的升降溫路徑。","textEn":"Measure rail temperature and longitudinal strain, record the fastening and maintenance history, and use spatially separated sensors to distinguish local heating from restrained segment behaviour. Calibrate remote readings against a contact rail thermometer, verify strain zero, and retain heating and cooling paths across the daily cycle.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出自由、部分拘束與完全拘束三種邊界，重算熱變形或應力，標明哪些輸入必須由鋼軌溫度及扣件試驗取得。 再以本單元 deltaT 的對照值重算 compression，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Draw free, partial and full restraint boundaries, recalculate expansion or stress, and identify inputs requiring rail-temperature measurements and fastener tests. Also recalculate compression for the alternative deltaT value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「長軌溫升與受限熱應力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long-rail temperature and restrained stress\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","側風翻覆力矩只和風速成正比而不涉及車體高度","量鋼軌本體溫度與縱向應變，記錄鎖定狀態和扣件維修歷程，用不同位置感測器區分局部溫差與整段受限變形。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Crosswind overturning moment is linear in wind speed and independent of vehicle height.","Measure rail temperature and longitudinal strain, record the fastening and maintenance history, and use spatially separated sensors to distinguish local heating from restrained segment behaviour."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量鋼軌本體溫度與縱向應變，記錄鎖定狀態和扣件維修歷程，用不同位置感測器區分局部溫差與整段受限變形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure rail temperature and longitudinal strain, record the fastening and maintenance history, and use spatially separated sensors to distinguish local heating from restrained segment behaviour. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b308-v16-24","title":"長軌溫升與受限熱應力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long-rail temperature and restrained stress: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「長軌溫升與受限熱應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Long-rail temperature and restrained stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把氣溫直接當成鋼軌溫度會錯估熱荷載；扣件鬆動可能降低局部軸力卻增加位移，不能據此宣稱整體穩定性改善。 需查鎖定軌溫紀錄，不能以當天最低氣溫當無應力點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Substituting air temperature misstates thermal loading; loose fasteners may reduce local force while increasing displacement, which does not prove improved overall stability. Check stress-free-temperature records rather than using the day’s minimum air temperature as the reference. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢查寒冬鋼軌降溫時應力方向與夏季熱壓縮的差別。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Examine the stress sign during winter cooling and contrast it with summer compression.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「完全拘束的鋼軌升溫仍會無應力地自由伸長」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A fully restrained rail still expands freely without stress when heated.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把氣溫直接當成鋼軌溫度會錯估熱荷載；扣件鬆動可能降低局部軸力卻增加位移，不能據此宣稱整體穩定性改善。 需查鎖定軌溫紀錄，不能以當天最低氣溫當無應力點。","textEn":"Substituting air temperature misstates thermal loading; loose fasteners may reduce local force while increasing displacement, which does not prove improved overall stability. Check stress-free-temperature records rather than using the day’s minimum air temperature as the reference.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「長軌溫升與受限熱應力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long-rail temperature and restrained stress\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把氣溫直接當成鋼軌溫度會錯估熱荷載；扣件鬆動可能降低局部軸力卻增加位移，不能據此宣稱整體穩定性改善。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","量測車速度提高時仍可永遠沿用原本取樣率"],"optionsEn":["Substituting air temperature misstates thermal loading.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","The original sampling rate remains sufficient at every increased inspection speed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把氣溫直接當成鋼軌溫度會錯估熱荷載；扣件鬆動可能降低局部軸力卻增加位移，不能據此宣稱整體穩定性改善。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Substituting air temperature misstates thermal loading; loose fasteners may reduce local force while increasing displacement, which does not prove improved overall stability. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b308-v16-s4","title":"空間波長與量測取樣與軸承故障頻率與轉速","titleEn":"Spatial wavelength and sampling & Bearing signatures and rotational speed","description":"本階段聚焦「空間波長與量測取樣」與「軸承故障頻率與轉速」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Spatial wavelength and sampling\" and \"Bearing signatures and rotational speed\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b308-v16-25","title":"空間波長與量測取樣：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Spatial wavelength and sampling: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「空間波長與量測取樣」如何影響東北新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Spatial wavelength and sampling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tohoku Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"移動量測車把軌道空間波長轉成時間頻率，速度除波長得到激振頻率。要避免混疊，取樣率需高於訊號頻寬兩倍並搭配抗混疊濾波；提高取樣率本身不能修正輪滑造成的里程誤差。 取樣頻率超過訊號最高頻率兩倍是重建的必要起點，仍需要抗混疊濾波及足夠振幅精度。尖峰與非平穩事件的要求不同，應從量測目的回推頻寬與記錄長度。 用列車通過雪害監測點的訊號決定所需取樣頻率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「空間波長與量測取樣」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A moving inspection vehicle converts track wavelength into temporal frequency through speed divided by wavelength. Avoiding aliasing requires a sampling rate above twice the signal bandwidth and an antialias filter. A higher sample rate alone cannot correct distance errors caused by wheel slip. Sampling above twice the highest signal frequency is a starting condition for reconstruction, but anti-alias filtering and amplitude accuracy remain necessary. Peaks and nonstationary events have different needs; derive bandwidth and recording duration from the measurement objective. Use passage signals at a snow-monitoring point to determine the required sampling frequency. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Spatial wavelength and sampling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：speed=50 m/s; wavelength=2 m；計算：nyquist_lower_bound=2*speed/wavelength=50 samples/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: speed=50 m/s; wavelength=2 m; calculation: nyquist_lower_bound=2*speed/wavelength=50 samples/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「量測車速度提高時仍可永遠沿用原本取樣率」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The original sampling rate remains sufficient at every increased inspection speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「空間波長與量測取樣」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Spatial wavelength and sampling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-25-k1","title":"空間波長與量測取樣","titleEn":"Spatial wavelength and sampling","text":"移動量測車把軌道空間波長轉成時間頻率，速度除波長得到激振頻率。要避免混疊，取樣率需高於訊號頻寬兩倍並搭配抗混疊濾波；提高取樣率本身不能修正輪滑造成的里程誤差。","textEn":"A moving inspection vehicle converts track wavelength into temporal frequency through speed divided by wavelength. Avoiding aliasing requires a sampling rate above twice the signal bandwidth and an antialias filter.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：量測車速度提高時仍可永遠沿用原本取樣率 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The original sampling rate remains sufficient at every increased inspection speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「空間波長與量測取樣」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Spatial wavelength and sampling\" is correct?","options":["量測車速度提高時仍可永遠沿用原本取樣率","移動量測車把軌道空間波長轉成時間頻率，速度除波長得到激振頻率。","頻譜中出現一個週期峰就一定證明軸承已損壞"],"optionsEn":["The original sampling rate remains sufficient at every increased inspection speed.","A moving inspection vehicle converts track wavelength into temporal frequency through speed divided by wavelength.","One periodic spectral peak necessarily proves that a bearing is damaged."],"answer":1,"explanation":"移動量測車把軌道空間波長轉成時間頻率，速度除波長得到激振頻率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A moving inspection vehicle converts track wavelength into temporal frequency through speed divided by wavelength. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b308-v16-26","title":"空間波長與量測取樣：定量估算","titleEn":"Spatial wavelength and sampling: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「空間波長與量測取樣」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Spatial wavelength and sampling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：speed=50 m/s; wavelength=2 m；計算：nyquist_lower_bound=2*speed/wavelength=50 samples/s。敏感度：speed 單獨增加百分之十至 55 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 55 samples/s。模型邊界：單一最短波長的理想Nyquist下界；實務需留濾波與取樣裕度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: speed=50 m/s; wavelength=2 m; calculation: nyquist_lower_bound=2*speed/wavelength=50 samples/s. Sensitivity: speed, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 55 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 55 samples/s. Model boundary: Ideal Nyquist lower bound for one shortest wavelength; practical filters and sampling need additional margin. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用已知波長的校驗訊號檢查量測鏈，對照獨立里程基準，並在不同車速下比較空間頻譜是否一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the chain with a known-wavelength reference, compare an independent distance datum, and inspect whether spatial spectra agree at different vehicle speeds.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：speed=50 m/s; wavelength=2 m；計算：nyquist_lower_bound=2*speed/wavelength=50 samples/s。敏感度：speed 單獨增加百分之十至 55 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 55 samples/s。模型邊界：單一最短波長的理想Nyquist下界；實務需留濾波與取樣裕度。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: speed=50 m/s; wavelength=2 m; calculation: nyquist_lower_bound=2*speed/wavelength=50 samples/s. Sensitivity: speed, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 55 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 55 samples/s. Model boundary: Ideal Nyquist lower bound for one shortest wavelength; practical filters and sampling need additional margin.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「空間波長與量測取樣」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Spatial wavelength and sampling\", which statement holds?","options":["濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好","電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：speed=50 m/s; wavelength=2 m。"],"optionsEn":["Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition.","A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：speed=50 m/s; wavelength=2 m；計算：nyquist_lower_bound=2*speed/wavelength=50 samples/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: speed=50 m/s; wavelength=2 m; calculation: nyquist_lower_bound=2*speed/wavelength=50 samples/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b308-v16-27","title":"空間波長與量測取樣：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Spatial wavelength and sampling: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「空間波長與量測取樣」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Spatial wavelength and sampling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用已知波長的校驗訊號檢查量測鏈，對照獨立里程基準，並在不同車速下比較空間頻譜是否一致。 用已知頻率訊號測試整條量測鏈，檢查抗混疊濾波器、時鐘誤差與遺漏樣本。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the chain with a known-wavelength reference, compare an independent distance datum, and inspect whether spatial spectra agree at different vehicle speeds. Test the complete measurement chain with a known-frequency signal, checking anti-alias filtering, clock error and missing samples. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把速度提高一成並把最短波長減半，計算取樣率需求，繪出混疊示意後提出抗混疊濾波的頻寬要求。 再以本單元 speed 的對照值重算 nyquist_lower_bound，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase speed by ten percent and halve the shortest wavelength, calculate sampling needs, illustrate aliasing, and specify the required antialias-filter bandwidth. Also recalculate nyquist_lower_bound for the alternative speed value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：不足取樣會把短波缺陷偽裝成長波，里程跳動又會改變重採樣位置；兩者需分別診斷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Undersampling disguises short-wave defects as long waves, while distance jumps alter resampling positions; the two mechanisms require separate diagnosis. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用已知波長的校驗訊號檢查量測鏈，對照獨立里程基準，並在不同車速下比較空間頻譜是否一致。 用已知頻率訊號測試整條量測鏈，檢查抗混疊濾波器、時鐘誤差與遺漏樣本。","textEn":"Check the chain with a known-wavelength reference, compare an independent distance datum, and inspect whether spatial spectra agree at different vehicle speeds. Test the complete measurement chain with a known-frequency signal, checking anti-alias filtering, clock error and missing samples.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把速度提高一成並把最短波長減半，計算取樣率需求，繪出混疊示意後提出抗混疊濾波的頻寬要求。 再以本單元 speed 的對照值重算 nyquist_lower_bound，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase speed by ten percent and halve the shortest wavelength, calculate sampling needs, illustrate aliasing, and specify the required antialias-filter bandwidth. Also recalculate nyquist_lower_bound for the alternative speed value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「空間波長與量測取樣」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Spatial wavelength and sampling\"?","options":["用已知波長的校驗訊號檢查量測鏈，對照獨立里程基準，並在不同車速下比較空間頻譜是否一致。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["Check the chain with a known-wavelength reference, compare an independent distance datum, and inspect whether spatial spectra agree at different vehicle speeds.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用已知波長的校驗訊號檢查量測鏈，對照獨立里程基準，並在不同車速下比較空間頻譜是否一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the chain with a known-wavelength reference, compare an independent distance datum, and inspect whether spatial spectra agree at different vehicle speeds. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b308-v16-28","title":"空間波長與量測取樣：失效診斷","titleEn":"Spatial wavelength and sampling: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「空間波長與量測取樣」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Spatial wavelength and sampling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不足取樣會把短波缺陷偽裝成長波，里程跳動又會改變重採樣位置；兩者需分別診斷。 降低取樣率後出現新低頻峰值，應先查混疊而非機械故障。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Undersampling disguises short-wave defects as long waves, while distance jumps alter resampling positions; the two mechanisms require separate diagnosis. A new low-frequency peak after downsampling requires checking aliasing before diagnosing a mechanical fault. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：用列車通過雪害監測點的訊號決定所需取樣頻率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Use passage signals at a snow-monitoring point to determine the required sampling frequency.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「量測車速度提高時仍可永遠沿用原本取樣率」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The original sampling rate remains sufficient at every increased inspection speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不足取樣會把短波缺陷偽裝成長波，里程跳動又會改變重採樣位置；兩者需分別診斷。 降低取樣率後出現新低頻峰值，應先查混疊而非機械故障。","textEn":"Undersampling disguises short-wave defects as long waves, while distance jumps alter resampling positions; the two mechanisms require separate diagnosis. A new low-frequency peak after downsampling requires checking aliasing before diagnosing a mechanical fault.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空間波長與量測取樣」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Spatial wavelength and sampling\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","不足取樣會把短波缺陷偽裝成長波，里程跳動又會改變重採樣位置；兩者需分別診斷。","頻譜中出現一個週期峰就一定證明軸承已損壞"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Undersampling disguises short-wave defects as long waves, while distance jumps alter resampling positions; the two mechanisms require separate diagnosis.","One periodic spectral peak necessarily proves that a bearing is damaged."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不足取樣會把短波缺陷偽裝成長波，里程跳動又會改變重採樣位置；兩者需分別診斷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Undersampling disguises short-wave defects as long waves, while distance jumps alter resampling positions; the two mechanisms require separate diagnosis. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b308-v16-29","title":"軸承故障頻率與轉速：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bearing signatures and rotational speed: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「軸承故障頻率與轉速」如何影響東北新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bearing signatures and rotational speed” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tohoku Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滾動軸承幾何決定故障衝擊相對轉速的頻率倍率，教學以已假設倍率乘轉速辨認階次。車速變動時固定頻率譜會展寬，階次追蹤可保留與轉速同步的訊號，但仍需排除輪軌激振。 幾何故障頻率是理想滾動關係，實際滑移會移動頻率或展寬峰值。量測頻譜需和當時轉速一起解讀，不能把固定頻率峰直接指派給某個故障部位。 把低溫黏度與軸承頻率特徵分開，避免直接由振幅推論損傷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「軸承故障頻率與轉速」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Bearing geometry determines fault-impact orders relative to rotational speed. Multiplying an assumed order by rotation frequency illustrates diagnosis. Variable speed smears fixed-frequency spectra; order tracking retains speed-synchronous signatures but must still distinguish wheel-rail excitation from bearing faults. Geometric defect frequencies assume ideal rolling; slip can shift or broaden peaks. Interpret the measured spectrum together with contemporaneous rotation speed instead of assigning a fixed peak directly to a defect location. Separate low-temperature lubrication effects from bearing frequency features instead of inferring damage from amplitude alone. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bearing signatures and rotational speed” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：rpm=600 rev/min; order=4.5 cycles/rev；計算：signature=rpm/60*order=45 Hz。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: rpm=600 rev/min; order=4.5 cycles/rev; calculation: signature=rpm/60*order=45 Hz.","failure":"常見誤解：「頻譜中出現一個週期峰就一定證明軸承已損壞」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One periodic spectral peak necessarily proves that a bearing is damaged.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「軸承故障頻率與轉速」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bearing signatures and rotational speed”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-29-k1","title":"軸承故障頻率與轉速","titleEn":"Bearing signatures and rotational speed","text":"滾動軸承幾何決定故障衝擊相對轉速的頻率倍率，教學以已假設倍率乘轉速辨認階次。車速變動時固定頻率譜會展寬，階次追蹤可保留與轉速同步的訊號，但仍需排除輪軌激振。","textEn":"Bearing geometry determines fault-impact orders relative to rotational speed. Multiplying an assumed order by rotation frequency illustrates diagnosis.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：頻譜中出現一個週期峰就一定證明軸承已損壞 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One periodic spectral peak necessarily proves that a bearing is damaged. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「軸承故障頻率與轉速」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bearing signatures and rotational speed\" is correct?","options":["頻譜中出現一個週期峰就一定證明軸承已損壞","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","滾動軸承幾何決定故障衝擊相對轉速的頻率倍率，教學以已假設倍率乘轉速辨認階次。"],"optionsEn":["One periodic spectral peak necessarily proves that a bearing is damaged.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","Bearing geometry determines fault-impact orders relative to rotational speed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滾動軸承幾何決定故障衝擊相對轉速的頻率倍率，教學以已假設倍率乘轉速辨認階次。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Bearing geometry determines fault-impact orders relative to rotational speed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b308-v16-30","title":"軸承故障頻率與轉速：定量估算","titleEn":"Bearing signatures and rotational speed: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「軸承故障頻率與轉速」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bearing signatures and rotational speed” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：rpm=600 rev/min; order=4.5 cycles/rev；計算：signature=rpm/60*order=45 Hz。敏感度：rpm 單獨增加百分之十至 660 rev/min，其餘固定，結果為 49.5 Hz。模型邊界：已知故障階次且轉速穩定；不代表某型軸承真實幾何。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: rpm=600 rev/min; order=4.5 cycles/rev; calculation: signature=rpm/60*order=45 Hz. Sensitivity: rpm, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 660 rev/min, with all other inputs fixed, gives 49.5 Hz. Model boundary: Assumed fault order and steady rotation; not the geometry of a particular bearing type. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步量測振動與轉速脈波，對比負載改變後的階次峰，並用溫度與潤滑紀錄作獨立佐證。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronise vibration and tachometer pulses, compare order peaks under changing load, and use temperature and lubrication records as independent corroboration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：rpm=600 rev/min; order=4.5 cycles/rev；計算：signature=rpm/60*order=45 Hz。敏感度：rpm 單獨增加百分之十至 660 rev/min，其餘固定，結果為 49.5 Hz。模型邊界：已知故障階次且轉速穩定；不代表某型軸承真實幾何。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: rpm=600 rev/min; order=4.5 cycles/rev; calculation: signature=rpm/60*order=45 Hz. Sensitivity: rpm, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 660 rev/min, with all other inputs fixed, gives 49.5 Hz. Model boundary: Assumed fault order and steady rotation; not the geometry of a particular bearing type.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「軸承故障頻率與轉速」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bearing signatures and rotational speed\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：rpm=600 rev/min; order=4.5 cycles/rev。","只要加熱器表面很熱就表示道岔冰雪問題已解決","側風翻覆力矩只和風速成正比而不涉及車體高度"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","A hot heater surface proves that snow and ice obstruction at the points is resolved.","Crosswind overturning moment is linear in wind speed and independent of vehicle height."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：rpm=600 rev/min; order=4.5 cycles/rev；計算：signature=rpm/60*order=45 Hz。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: rpm=600 rev/min; order=4.5 cycles/rev; calculation: signature=rpm/60*order=45 Hz. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b308-v16-31","title":"軸承故障頻率與轉速：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bearing signatures and rotational speed: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「軸承故障頻率與轉速」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bearing signatures and rotational speed” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步量測振動與轉速脈波，對比負載改變後的階次峰，並用溫度與潤滑紀錄作獨立佐證。 以獨立轉速計核對每段資料，保留頻譜解析度和窗函數，並比較不同轉速的階次。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronise vibration and tachometer pulses, compare order peaks under changing load, and use temperature and lubrication records as independent corroboration. Verify each data segment with an independent tachometer, retain spectral resolution and window function, and compare orders across rotation speeds. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用兩種轉速檢查同一峰是否維持固定階次，再加入輪軌接縫頻率，比較哪些特徵能區分故障來源。 再以本單元 rpm 的對照值重算 signature，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Use two speeds to test whether a peak maintains constant order, add a rail-joint excitation frequency, and compare features that distinguish the sources. Also recalculate signature for the alternative rpm value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：輪扁或軌道接縫也能產生週期衝擊，單一頻譜峰不能唯一定位軸承損傷；速度估計錯誤則會使階次偏移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wheel flats and track joints also create periodic impacts, so one spectral peak cannot uniquely identify bearing damage; wrong speed estimates shift calculated orders. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步量測振動與轉速脈波，對比負載改變後的階次峰，並用溫度與潤滑紀錄作獨立佐證。 以獨立轉速計核對每段資料，保留頻譜解析度和窗函數，並比較不同轉速的階次。","textEn":"Synchronise vibration and tachometer pulses, compare order peaks under changing load, and use temperature and lubrication records as independent corroboration. Verify each data segment with an independent tachometer, retain spectral resolution and window function, and compare orders across rotation speeds.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用兩種轉速檢查同一峰是否維持固定階次，再加入輪軌接縫頻率，比較哪些特徵能區分故障來源。 再以本單元 rpm 的對照值重算 signature，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Use two speeds to test whether a peak maintains constant order, add a rail-joint excitation frequency, and compare features that distinguish the sources. Also recalculate signature for the alternative rpm value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「軸承故障頻率與轉速」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bearing signatures and rotational speed\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","同步量測振動與轉速脈波，對比負載改變後的階次峰，並用溫度與潤滑紀錄作獨立佐證。","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Synchronise vibration and tachometer pulses, compare order peaks under changing load, and use temperature and lubrication records as independent corroboration.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同步量測振動與轉速脈波，對比負載改變後的階次峰，並用溫度與潤滑紀錄作獨立佐證。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronise vibration and tachometer pulses, compare order peaks under changing load, and use temperature and lubrication records as independent corroboration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b308-v16-32","title":"軸承故障頻率與轉速：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bearing signatures and rotational speed: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「軸承故障頻率與轉速」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bearing signatures and rotational speed” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"輪扁或軌道接縫也能產生週期衝擊，單一頻譜峰不能唯一定位軸承損傷；速度估計錯誤則會使階次偏移。 速度改變後峰值若不隨階次移動，須檢查其他激振來源。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wheel flats and track joints also create periodic impacts, so one spectral peak cannot uniquely identify bearing damage; wrong speed estimates shift calculated orders. If a peak does not track rotational order as speed changes, inspect other excitation sources. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把低溫黏度與軸承頻率特徵分開，避免直接由振幅推論損傷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Separate low-temperature lubrication effects from bearing frequency features instead of inferring damage from amplitude alone.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「頻譜中出現一個週期峰就一定證明軸承已損壞」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One periodic spectral peak necessarily proves that a bearing is damaged.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"輪扁或軌道接縫也能產生週期衝擊，單一頻譜峰不能唯一定位軸承損傷；速度估計錯誤則會使階次偏移。 速度改變後峰值若不隨階次移動，須檢查其他激振來源。","textEn":"Wheel flats and track joints also create periodic impacts, so one spectral peak cannot uniquely identify bearing damage; wrong speed estimates shift calculated orders. If a peak does not track rotational order as speed changes, inspect other excitation sources.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「軸承故障頻率與轉速」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bearing signatures and rotational speed\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","輪扁或軌道接縫也能產生週期衝擊，單一頻譜峰不能唯一定位軸承損傷；速度估計錯誤則會使階次偏移。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","Wheel flats and track joints also create periodic impacts, so one spectral peak cannot uniquely identify bearing damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"輪扁或軌道接縫也能產生週期衝擊，單一頻譜峰不能唯一定位軸承損傷；速度估計錯誤則會使階次偏移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wheel flats and track joints also create periodic impacts, so one spectral peak cannot uniquely identify bearing damage; wrong speed estimates shift calculated orders. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b308-v16-s5","title":"延遲與制動距離與濾網壓差與通風功率","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance & Filter pressure drop and fan power","description":"本階段聚焦「延遲與制動距離」與「濾網壓差與通風功率」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Delay and braking distance\" and \"Filter pressure drop and fan power\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b308-v16-33","title":"延遲與制動距離：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「延遲與制動距離」如何影響東北新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Delay and braking distance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tohoku Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。速度平方項說明高速時少量速度誤差會被放大，固定減速度只能作第一輪界限估算。 延遲項與速度成正比，減速項與速度平方成正比；把兩項分開後，才能選擇改善控制延遲或增加有效制動的方案。若存在坡度，應另加沿坡重力，不能只改總距離。 對降雪後低黏著情境重新估算制動距離的保守界限。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「延遲與制動距離」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds. Only the deceleration phase removes kinetic energy, so stopping distance includes both a delay term and a braking term. The squared speed dependence amplifies speed uncertainty; constant deceleration is only an initial bounding approximation. The delay term is linear in speed and the deceleration term is quadratic. Separating them reveals whether control latency or effective braking deserves attention. A gradient requires an added gravitational component, not an arbitrary adjustment to the final distance. Re-estimate a conservative braking-distance bound for reduced adhesion after snowfall. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Delay and braking distance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「延遲與制動距離」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Delay and braking distance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-33-k1","title":"延遲與制動距離","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance","text":"列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。速度平方項說明高速時少量速度誤差會被放大，固定減速度只能作第一輪界限估算。","textEn":"A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds. Only the deceleration phase removes kinetic energy, so stopping distance includes both a delay term and a braking term.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「延遲與制動距離」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Delay and braking distance\" is correct?","options":["列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。","速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成","濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好"],"optionsEn":["A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds.","A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.","Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"列車在控制命令傳遞與煞車建立期間仍向前行駛，減速段才把動能耗散；因此停車距離包含延遲距離與減速距離。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A train continues moving while the command propagates and brake force builds. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b308-v16-34","title":"延遲與制動距離：定量估算","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「延遲與制動距離」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Delay and braking distance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 77 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 4427.5 m。模型邊界：水平直線、定減速、無風；沒有建立黏著分布與煞車熱衰退。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 77 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 4427.5 m. Model boundary: Level straight track and constant deceleration; adhesion variation and thermal fade are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m。敏感度：v 單獨增加百分之十至 77 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 4427.5 m。模型邊界：水平直線、定減速、無風；沒有建立黏著分布與煞車熱衰退。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m. Sensitivity: v, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 77 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 4427.5 m. Model boundary: Level straight track and constant deceleration; adhesion variation and thermal fade are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「延遲與制動距離」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Delay and braking distance\", which statement holds?","options":["電機額定扭矩夠大就不需要考慮輪軌黏著","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2。","隧道壓力波必定與列車以相同速度到達出口"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large rated motor torque eliminates the need to consider wheel-rail adhesion.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A tunnel pressure wave necessarily reaches the portal at the same speed as the train."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2；計算：distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=70 m/s; delay=2.5 s; a=0.7 m/s^2; calculation: distance=v*delay+v*v/(2*a)=3675 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b308-v16-35","title":"延遲與制動距離：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「延遲與制動距離」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Delay and braking distance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。 用獨立里程或地速核對輪速積分，報告濕乾軌差異及停車距離的重複試驗範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps. Identify command delay separately from steady deceleration and cross-check distance by integrating measured speed. Check integrated wheel speed against independent distance or ground speed, and report wet-dry differences and repeated stopping-distance ranges. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：分別增加延遲與初速，畫出兩條停車曲線；寫出哪個區段對各參數敏感，以及需要哪些現場資料才可建立保護曲線。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 distance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase delay and initial speed separately, plot both stopping curves, identify the sensitive phase, and list the field evidence needed before defining a protection curve. Also recalculate distance for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。 用獨立里程或地速核對輪速積分，報告濕乾軌差異及停車距離的重複試驗範圍。","textEn":"Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps. Identify command delay separately from steady deceleration and cross-check distance by integrating measured speed. Check integrated wheel speed against independent distance or ground speed, and report wet-dry differences and repeated stopping-distance ranges.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"分別增加延遲與初速，畫出兩條停車曲線；寫出哪個區段對各參數敏感，以及需要哪些現場資料才可建立保護曲線。 再以本單元 v 的對照值重算 distance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase delay and initial speed separately, plot both stopping curves, identify the sensitive phase, and list the field evidence needed before defining a protection curve. Also recalculate distance for the alternative v value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「延遲與制動距離」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Delay and braking distance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","完全拘束的鋼軌升溫仍會無應力地自由伸長","對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A fully restrained rail still expands freely without stress when heated.","Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對齊速度、煞車缸壓力與里程的時間戳，分開辨識命令延遲及穩態減速度，再以積分速度的距離交叉檢查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align speed, brake-cylinder pressure and distance timestamps. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b308-v16-36","title":"延遲與制動距離：失效診斷","titleEn":"Delay and braking distance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「延遲與制動距離」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Delay and braking distance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 應比較壓力建立與地速下降先後，避免誤判煞車故障。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. Compare pressure build-up with ground-speed decay before diagnosing a brake fault. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：對降雪後低黏著情境重新估算制動距離的保守界限。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Re-estimate a conservative braking-distance bound for reduced adhesion after snowfall.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「速度增加一成時制動距離必定也只增加一成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A ten percent speed increase must increase braking distance by only ten percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 應比較壓力建立與地速下降先後，避免誤判煞車故障。","textEn":"Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. Compare pressure build-up with ground-speed decay before diagnosing a brake fault.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「延遲與制動距離」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Delay and braking distance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好"],"optionsEn":["Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition."],"answer":0,"explanation":"輪滑保護介入與濕軌會降低實際減速度；感測時間不同步也能製造假延遲，須以第二個時鐘和輪速紀錄區分。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wheel-slide protection and wet rails can reduce deceleration; unsynchronised sensors can imitate a delay, requiring an independent clock and wheel-speed records. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b308-v16-37","title":"濾網壓差與通風功率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Filter pressure drop and fan power: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「濾網壓差與通風功率」如何影響東北新幹線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Filter pressure drop and fan power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tohoku Shinkansen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"風機必須克服風道與濾網壓差才能輸送空氣，輸入功率近似為壓差乘體積流率再除效率。積塵提高阻力但工作點會沿風機曲線改變，因此固定風量假設只是一種受控比較。 風機功率等於壓力差乘體積流率再除以宣告效率，壓力與流量必須使用同一工作點。積塵使阻力和風機工作點共同改變，固定流量算例不能預測未控制風量時的耗電。 比較進氣濾材積雪前後壓差，檢查量測是否受風量改變干擾。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「濾網壓差與通風功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A fan must overcome duct and filter pressure losses to move air. Input power is approximately pressure rise times volume flow divided by efficiency. Dust raises resistance but shifts the operating point on the fan curve, so fixed flow is only a controlled comparison. Fan power equals pressure difference times volume flow divided by the declared efficiency. Pressure and flow must refer to one operating point. Dust changes resistance and the fan operating point together, so a fixed-flow example cannot predict consumption without airflow control. Compare intake-filter pressure drop before and after snow accumulation and control for airflow changes. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Filter pressure drop and fan power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1；計算：fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1; calculation: fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W.","failure":"常見誤解：「濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「濾網壓差與通風功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Filter pressure drop and fan power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-37-k1","title":"濾網壓差與通風功率","titleEn":"Filter pressure drop and fan power","text":"風機必須克服風道與濾網壓差才能輸送空氣，輸入功率近似為壓差乘體積流率再除效率。積塵提高阻力但工作點會沿風機曲線改變，因此固定風量假設只是一種受控比較。","textEn":"A fan must overcome duct and filter pressure losses to move air. Input power is approximately pressure rise times volume flow divided by efficiency.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「濾網壓差與通風功率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Filter pressure drop and fan power\" is correct?","options":["濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好","風機必須克服風道與濾網壓差才能輸送空氣，輸入功率近似為壓差乘體積流率再除效率。","只要加熱器表面很熱就表示道岔冰雪問題已解決"],"optionsEn":["Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition.","A fan must overcome duct and filter pressure losses to move air.","A hot heater surface proves that snow and ice obstruction at the points is resolved."],"answer":1,"explanation":"風機必須克服風道與濾網壓差才能輸送空氣，輸入功率近似為壓差乘體積流率再除效率。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A fan must overcome duct and filter pressure losses to move air. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b308-v16-38","title":"濾網壓差與通風功率：定量估算","titleEn":"Filter pressure drop and fan power: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「濾網壓差與通風功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Filter pressure drop and fan power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1；計算：fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W。敏感度：pressure 單獨增加百分之十至 385 Pa，其餘固定，結果為 1604.167 W。模型邊界：固定風量與總效率；不包含風機曲線移動和馬達熱限制。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1; calculation: fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W. Sensitivity: pressure, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 385 Pa, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1604.167 W. Model boundary: Fixed flow and overall efficiency; fan-curve shifts and motor thermal limits are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時量濾網前後壓差、實際風量和電功率，用乾淨濾網建立基準，並記錄沙塵、濕度與維修時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure differential pressure, actual flow and input power together, establish a clean-filter baseline, and record dust exposure, humidity and maintenance timing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1；計算：fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W。敏感度：pressure 單獨增加百分之十至 385 Pa，其餘固定，結果為 1604.167 W。模型邊界：固定風量與總效率；不包含風機曲線移動和馬達熱限制。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1; calculation: fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W. Sensitivity: pressure, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 385 Pa, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1604.167 W. Model boundary: Fixed flow and overall efficiency; fan-curve shifts and motor thermal limits are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「濾網壓差與通風功率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Filter pressure drop and fan power\", which statement holds?","options":["側風翻覆力矩只和風速成正比而不涉及車體高度","地震預警成功觸發就代表列車必能在強震前完全停下","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1。"],"optionsEn":["Crosswind overturning moment is linear in wind speed and independent of vehicle height.","A successfully triggered earthquake warning guarantees a complete stop before strong shaking.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1；計算：fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: pressure=350 Pa; flow=2.5 m^3/s; eta=0.6 1; calculation: fan_power=pressure*flow/eta=1458.333 W. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b308-v16-39","title":"濾網壓差與通風功率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Filter pressure drop and fan power: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「濾網壓差與通風功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Filter pressure drop and fan power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時量濾網前後壓差、實際風量和電功率，用乾淨濾網建立基準，並記錄沙塵、濕度與維修時間。 校正取壓點與風量計，同步量測電功率，核對效率是否包含馬達與驅動器損失。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure differential pressure, actual flow and input power together, establish a clean-filter baseline, and record dust exposure, humidity and maintenance timing. Calibrate pressure taps and airflow measurement, record electric power simultaneously, and check whether efficiency includes motor and drive losses. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對堵塞與旁路兩個情境列出壓差、風量和粒子濃度的預期方向，設計三項量測共同判斷而非只靠單一數字。 再以本單元 pressure 的對照值重算 fan_power，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Predict pressure drop, airflow and particle concentration for clogging and bypass scenarios, then design a three-measurement diagnosis instead of relying on one number. Also recalculate fan_power for the alternative pressure value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：旁路漏氣可能讓壓差降低但過濾品質變差；只以壓差低判定良好，會忽略濾網破損和密封失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Bypass leakage may lower pressure drop while worsening filtration; a low drop alone can therefore hide a damaged filter or failed seal. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時量濾網前後壓差、實際風量和電功率，用乾淨濾網建立基準，並記錄沙塵、濕度與維修時間。 校正取壓點與風量計，同步量測電功率，核對效率是否包含馬達與驅動器損失。","textEn":"Measure differential pressure, actual flow and input power together, establish a clean-filter baseline, and record dust exposure, humidity and maintenance timing. Calibrate pressure taps and airflow measurement, record electric power simultaneously, and check whether efficiency includes motor and drive losses.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對堵塞與旁路兩個情境列出壓差、風量和粒子濃度的預期方向，設計三項量測共同判斷而非只靠單一數字。 再以本單元 pressure 的對照值重算 fan_power，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Predict pressure drop, airflow and particle concentration for clogging and bypass scenarios, then design a three-measurement diagnosis instead of relying on one number. Also recalculate fan_power for the alternative pressure value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「濾網壓差與通風功率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Filter pressure drop and fan power\"?","options":["同時量濾網前後壓差、實際風量和電功率，用乾淨濾網建立基準，並記錄沙塵、濕度與維修時間。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","量測車速度提高時仍可永遠沿用原本取樣率"],"optionsEn":["Measure differential pressure, actual flow and input power together, establish a clean-filter baseline, and record dust exposure, humidity and maintenance timing.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The original sampling rate remains sufficient at every increased inspection speed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時量濾網前後壓差、實際風量和電功率，用乾淨濾網建立基準，並記錄沙塵、濕度與維修時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure differential pressure, actual flow and input power together, establish a clean-filter baseline, and record dust exposure, humidity and maintenance timing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b308-v16-40","title":"濾網壓差與通風功率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Filter pressure drop and fan power: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b308-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「濾網壓差與通風功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Filter pressure drop and fan power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"旁路漏氣可能讓壓差降低但過濾品質變差；只以壓差低判定良好，會忽略濾網破損和密封失效。 壓差很低也可能是旁通，須核對濾材密封及實際風量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Bypass leakage may lower pressure drop while worsening filtration; a low drop alone can therefore hide a damaged filter or failed seal. Very low pressure drop can indicate bypass; check filter sealing and actual airflow. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較進氣濾材積雪前後壓差，檢查量測是否受風量改變干擾。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare intake-filter pressure drop before and after snow accumulation and control for airflow changes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「濾網壓差越低就一定表示過濾狀況越好」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower filter pressure drop always means better filtration condition.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b308-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"旁路漏氣可能讓壓差降低但過濾品質變差；只以壓差低判定良好，會忽略濾網破損和密封失效。 壓差很低也可能是旁通，須核對濾材密封及實際風量。","textEn":"Bypass leakage may lower pressure drop while worsening filtration; a low drop alone can therefore hide a damaged filter or failed seal. Very low pressure drop can indicate bypass; check filter sealing and actual airflow.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]},{"id":"b308-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「濾網壓差與通風功率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Filter pressure drop and fan power\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","旁路漏氣可能讓壓差降低但過濾品質變差；只以壓差低判定良好，會忽略濾網破損和密封失效。","只要加熱器表面很熱就表示道岔冰雪問題已解決"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Bypass leakage may lower pressure drop while worsening filtration; a low drop alone can therefore hide a damaged filter or failed seal.","A hot heater surface proves that snow and ice obstruction at the points is resolved."],"answer":1,"explanation":"旁路漏氣可能讓壓差降低但過濾品質變差；只以壓差低判定良好，會忽略濾網破損和密封失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Bypass leakage may lower pressure drop while worsening filtration; a low drop alone can therefore hide a damaged filter or failed seal. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-b308-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b308-background"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b308-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b308-en.svg"}};
